# Intent: The speech bubble (owner request 2026-11-16): the setting speech_bubble (off by default, on for the Stock style until a person chooses) shows what the unit says in a rounded bubble at the bottom of the screen, never over the eyes. The words come from the sentence messages the unit already receives (the captions path); a mute, vision-off or full quiet look hides them. The bubble is a label with no scrolling: it is wrapped to at most two lines, sized to the text, drawn when a sentence arrives and when a page turns, and a sentence longer than two lines is paged at word boundaries (the page time follows its length, 1.6 to 3.5 s); the last sentence stays 2.6 s and the bubble fades in four steps. Turning the setting off clears the words on screen. Costs: one redraw per sentence, no per frame text layout (the old circular scrolling label redrew every frame), a short string vector per sentence.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/{speech_bubble.cpp,default.h} (MIT) and hal/maipai_face.cc (maipai_face_captions_on)
# Check after a flash: self.prefs.set speech_bubble true, then a spoken turn: the sentences appear in the bubble and fade after the last; a two sentence reply pages; mute hides it; the Stock style shows it on a unit that never chose.

